{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310596,"nonce":"UR+2LyFUEfx4tzoDh9MknSGw8og=","title":"A Map keyed by an enum with a constructor parameter costs 1.27 GB in a 7-line program, and OOM-kills the compiler on Issue2479","message":"Seven lines, 1.27 GB peak RSS:\n\n    enum EFoo { Foo(a:Int); }\n    class A { static function main() {\n        var map:Map\u003cEFoo, Int\u003e = [];\n        map[Foo(1)] = 1;\n        Sys.println(map[Foo(1)]);\n    } }\n\nNormal is ~59 MB. NARROWED — all of these are normal, so the trigger is the\ncombination, not any one part:\n\n    Map\u003cString,Int\u003e                       59 MB\n    Map\u003cType.ValueType,String\u003e            59 MB\n    Map\u003cK,Int\u003e with a CLASS key           59 MB\n    Map\u003cEBar,Int\u003e, enum with NO parameter 59 MB\n    parameterised enum, no Map at all     63 MB\n    Map\u003cEFoo,Int\u003e DECLARED but not used   63 MB\n    Map\u003cEFoo,Int\u003e USED, Foo(a:Int)      1270 MB   \u003c-- 21x\n\nCorpus `Issue2479` combines it with a second enum-keyed map and reaches a\n**61.2 GB peak memory footprint**, at which point the OS SIGKILLs it — one of\nonly two tests in the corpus that die by signal 9. `Issue2889` is the other.\nBoth die during COMPILATION, before any output past the banner.\n\nMeasure it with the redirect order right, or you get nothing:\n    /usr/bin/time -l \u003ccmd\u003e 2\u003e\u00261 \u003e/dev/null | awk '/maximum resident/...'\n`{ cmd \u003e/dev/null 2\u003e/dev/null; } 2\u003e\u00261` swallows time's own report. On a run that\ndies by signal, macOS prints `peak memory footprint` but NOT `maximum resident\nset size`, so grep for both.\n\nNot yet root-caused. The shape suggests runaway monomorphisation over the enum's\nparameter type, since a parameterless enum key is free.\n\nSee [[bugs_conformance_crash_timeout_bimodality_in_ci]] for why these show up as\nTIMEOUT rather than CRASH on some CI runs.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_enum_keyed_map_allocation_blowup` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}